{"data":{"repository":{"pullRequest":{"title":"ledger/cmd/grpc: upload exports with gotools' aws-sdk-go-v2 uploader","body":"Moves export uploads to the aws-sdk-go-v2 uploader in gotools' `snapshot` package (tamarinworks/gotools#438, moved into `snapshot` itself by tamarinworks/gotools#439). aws-sdk-go-v2 honours `AWS_ENDPOINT_URL_S3`, which the local dev scripts already set, so local exports can go to LocalStack's `exports` bucket (tamarinworks/bedrock#2417) instead of real S3. Follows tamarinworks/gotools#431.\n\n- Bumps gotools to the tamarinworks/gotools#439 merge. aws-sdk-go v1 is now only an indirect dependency.\n- Replaces the ledger's aws-sdk-go v1 uploader with `snapshot.NewS3Uploader`, passing the region and keys from config. gotools keeps the same rule as before: static credentials only when both keys are set.\n- Drops the tracing wrapper around the uploader. S3 requests now show up as HTTP client spans, but the upload span and its bucket and key fields go.\n- Registering the export server now returns an error, which `Run` passes to `log.MustSucceed`.\n- The cron server takes a `snapshot.Uploader`, and the test fake implements `UploadObject` instead of the v1 `UploadWithContext`. Nothing outside atrium builds the cron server, so no other service needs code changes, but lily needs an atrium bump after this merges to pick up the new uploader.\n\nLocal development only switches to LocalStack once tamarinworks/tamarin-chef#3572 points the exports bucket at it.\n","author":{"login":"tam-fairweather"},"baseRefName":"master","baseRefOid":"bb9f3db3f2055c8c9e40350be1e04050d9879274","headRefOid":"7695ee9f229863c890514e3e7fcf1c33be9ca13c","mergeable":"UNKNOWN","commits":{"nodes":[{"commit":{"oid":"7695ee9f229863c890514e3e7fcf1c33be9ca13c","statusCheckRollup":{"state":"SUCCESS","contexts":{"nodes":[{"__typename":"StatusContext","context":"ci/circleci: build","state":"SUCCESS","targetUrl":"https://circleci.com/gh/tamarinworks/atrium/48475"},{"__typename":"StatusContex